statement:
The modified SQG equation reads

\begin{aligned}
\partial_t\theta +u\cdot \nabla\theta &=0, \\
u &= \mathcal{R}^\perp|\nabla|^{-\varepsilon}\theta,
\end{aligned}
where $\theta: \mathbb{R}\times\mathbb{R}^2\to\mathbb{R}$, $\varepsilon>0$, and $\mathcal{R}$ is the Riesz transform. Is it possible to find global weak solutions to when $\varepsilon=0$, with respect to random initial data ?

